===Noun===
{{en-noun|demonocracies}}

# {{context|fiction}} A [[government]] by [[demon]]s, be it in a spiritual or temporal sense. This can refer both to the demonic hierarchy's governance of Hell, or the spiritual governance which demons exercise over those on earth who are in their thrall. It also refers to a political system some Satanists and demonolators believe will be established at the end of the age, in which all temporal powers of governance are exercised by demons, speaking through their appointed priests and priestesses on the earth. (Akin to "theocracy", except the priests are not of god but rather of demons.)
# {{pejorative}} [[democracy|Democracy]], used by those who believe that government by the people is no better than government by the devils of hell, or worse.
# {{pejorative}} used to describe the perceived misuse of the term "[[democracy|Democracy]]"

In finance, demonocracy describes any situation where private firms/individuals have more influence on the wealth of the middle classes than democratically elected officials in government. An example would be the banks that control the unregulated derivatives market. In a more general sense, demonocracy is any force (finance/war/information) that has more influence on socio-political systems than the government. An example would be a terrorist organisation such as the IRA using force of arms to secure prominent political positions in Northern Ireland. Or Private Manning altering the political landscape and everyday life through the power of information. Small groups with massive power.

===Usage notes===
"Oppose and disagree, destroy [[demonocracy]]" is a line from the Muse song "Assassin" (on the 2006 [[w:Black Holes and Revelations|Black Holes and Revelations]] album)